index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..65c29c4498c12ada84e3d3e8d94da061a2595938
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/gguf-mxfp8-prefill.md
@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@
+# Experimental MXFP8 GGUF prefill
+
+Set `NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_MXFP8=1` before starting the process to enable this
+explicit, lossy numerical profile. Unset or `0` retains the existing q8_1 path.
+The switch is immutable after its first query and must precede workspace planning.
+Use `NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_NVFP4=0` when qualifying FP8 alone. The stored model
+weights and selected KV representation are unchanged.
+
+## Supported calls and routes
+
+The experiment supports an sm120 image on compute capability 12.x, positive K
+divisible by 256, and IQ3_XXS, IQ3_S, IQ2_XXS, IQ2_XS, IQ2_S, IQ4_XS, Q2_K and
+Q4_K. Unsupported devices/formats and calls below 256 columns retain the existing
+route. Supported decode/verification batches are at most 128 columns and remain
+on q8_1. Prefill errors can still affect later KV/GDN state and generated output.
+
+- At 256 through 1023 columns, the default fused 128-row by 128-column tile uses producer
+  warps with cp.async staging and native block-scaled E4M3 MMA consumer warps.
+  Results pass directly through the existing store, residual or gate epilogue.
+- At 1024 columns and above, a bounded weight image feeds cuBLASLt. GEMM
+  accumulation is FP32. Aligned BF16 Store/Add destinations receive BF16 directly; FP32 and gated outputs retain the existing FP32 epilogue path.
+  Each 32-byte image slice is written as two aligned 128-bit stores. This keeps
+  the scalar decoder's exact FP8 bytes/scales and the existing 64 MiB slab limit;
+  it adds no model copy, codebook allocation or workspace. Independent weight
+  codec tests cover all eight formats, signed/zero/subnormal/maximal finite
+  scales, padded rows and real K, alongside public-Op FP64 and Graph checks.
+
+The backend's existing device profiles can select the Q8 integer matrix route
+instead of the tile. Keys are `gguf_prefill_mxfp8/<format>/<N>x<K>/<epilogue>`;
+the four epilogues are `f32`, `bf16`, `bf16-add` and `bf16-silu`. Q8 overrides
+require whole 128-row tiles; unsupported formats, partial row tiles and other
+epilogues keep their existing route. A Q8 choice bypasses both FP8 kernels and
+the two-stage Lt path. T >= 1024 retains Lt irrespective of these profile keys.
+
+At exactly T=512 a measured `lt` entry may select the same bounded cuBLASLt
+implementation used at T>=1024. Workspace queries include its slab only when a
+matching entry can be reached in the requested extent interval. The FP32 weight
+decode, actual group amax, E4M3/E8M0 representation and FP32 accumulation are
+retained; GEMM reduction order may differ from the tile implementation.
+
+The 36-SM RTX 5060 Ti table has 78 T=512 entries for IQ3_S/IQ4_XS across ten
+registered shapes and four epilogues. Two mirrored five-trial median public-Op
+sweeps confirmed each retained improvement above 3%. IQ3_S 1024x5120 BF16 Store
+and Add retain tile because Lt regressed. Existing T=256 choices are preserved;
+the entries stop at 512, with tile retained through 511. Other cards and
+unmeasured shapes retain their current routing and workspace requirements.
+The automatic calibration tool currently measures this namespace at T=256;
+it does not yet generate the Lt512 entries. These built-ins came from the
+separately qualified native public-Op sweep.
+
+The first built-in set has 25 entries for the 36-SM RTX 5060 Ti, at exactly
+T=256. Two independent native calibrations measured 8 formats, 10 actual-model
+shapes and 4 epilogues; only Q8 winners confirmed in both runs were retained.
+Every run uses an 11-sample median, a 3% selection margin, interleaved confirmation
+and the existing 5% peak-output-difference rejection. The qualification test also
+uses an independent CPU/FP64 oracle. A win for one epilogue does not select the
+others. Other devices and unmeasured widths keep their previous choices; no
+5060 Ti SM-fill threshold is applied to them. User-calibrated profiles retain
+their normal per-key priority over built-ins.
+
+Adding this family does not discard previously calibrated non-FP8 routes. The
+loader recognizes only the verified additive catalog transition, excludes the
+new namespace from old provenance, and preserves unrelated old measurements
+when a partial FP8 calibration is stored. Missing provenance and other catalog
+mismatches retain their rejection behavior. Volta/Turing catalogs are unchanged.
+
+To measure this optional family on another supported device, set MXFP8=1 and run
+`ninfer-calibrate --only gguf_prefill_mxfp8/ --detail --repeat 11`.
+The normal profile schema, hardware/SM matching and route-catalog provenance
+apply. The family is skipped when MXFP8 is disabled or unsupported. Calibrate
+while the GPU is idle, then qualify full-model speed and quality before using
+the measured choices. Synthetic Op measurements alone do not prove a model win.
+
+## Numerical and resource boundaries
+
+Activations, after their optional column gather, and decoded FP32 weights use
+one E4M3 representation and one UE8M0 power-of-two scale per 32 values. The scale
+is `2^ceil(log2(amax/448))`, clamped to the finite UE8M0 range. All-zero groups use
+scale one. The encoder uses round-to-nearest-even and finite saturation.
+
+The five grid i-quants decode raw selectors through lookup entries carrying the
+actual maximum selector. This preserves actual per-group amax, signed scales
+and direct FP32-to-E4M3 rounding. Other supported types retain their FP32 value
+decoder. There is no FP16 weight intermediate or type-range-bound replacement.
+MMA accumulates in FP32. Dynamic shared-memory attributes are initialized per
+CUDA device; this is independent of the runtime stream or CUDA Graph.
+
+All activation, scale, padded-output, fallback and weight-image storage is
+caller-owned and included in workspace planning. The cuBLASLt weight image is
+capped at 64 MiB except for a minimum 128-row tile, rather than a full-model FP8
+copy. Its larger slab and FP32 output plane cost more transient storage than
+the historical 8 MiB implementation. Tile-only plans do not reserve an unused
+cuBLASLt slab. cuBLASLt plans are cached per device and geometry.
+
+The enabled Qwen prefill signature and all-family snapshot binding identify
+`mxfp8-e4m3-e8m0-f32-profile-v2` plus the ordered FP8 routing bands of every
+device rank. This deliberately invalidates older FP8 state/cost bindings and
+separates custom Q8/tile mixtures. Default Q8 signatures are unchanged. State
+from a different numerical profile must not be treated as interchangeable.
+
+## Qualification and use
+
+Independent CPU packed-GGUF decoders, a CPU E4M3 encoder and naive FP64 products
+qualify represented operands, including gathers, tails, extreme scales, stores,
+residual/gated epilogues, graph replay and a large slab boundary. Encoded-operand
+accuracy does not measure the quantization loss against the original model;
+model perplexity and request behavior are separate acceptance evidence.
+The route tests cover FP8/Q8 products sharing an input and workspace, gather,
+real N/K shapes, width/format/epilogue limits, canaries and numerical signatures.
+`ninfer_linear_gguf_mxfp8_test --two-device` additionally checks that a route
+installed on one device does not affect the other and that signature collection
+restores the calling thread's device. This is not tensor-parallel qualification.
+
+Mixed routing retains the conservative Q8-plus-FP8 workspace capacity bound;
+it does not reduce the maximum allocation or create a persistent repacked model.
+Q8 and FP8 products can require two activation layouts for the same input. That
+extra conversion is included in full-Op and full-model timings. FP8 remains a
+lossy opt-in even where a measured shape now uses the more accurate Q8 operands.
+
+```powershell
+$env:NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_MXFP8 = '1'
+$env:NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_NVFP4 = '0'
+.\ninfer-serve.exe MODEL.ninfer --prefill-chunk 256
+```
+
+Restart with MXFP8 set to `0` to use q8_1. This remains default-off and
+experimental. The former two-pass-only 8 MiB implementation and its timings
+are historical, and do not describe this fused-tile implementation.
+
+The pipeline is adapted from `2-com-org/ninfer-5060-qwen` at
+`08c4fb70bec11063cae42eafe1c1b0dc3a7f993e`. Local actual-amax scaling, FP32
+interpretation and output boundaries differ from that repository's optimized
+scale-bound and some FP16/BF16 paths. Its numerical and performance results
+cannot substitute for qualification of this implementation.
+
+## Route-owned workspace and BF16 output
+
+Workspace planning covers every token width in the requested interval, including
+profile-specific Lt512 and tail fallbacks. Tile-only calls need no generic FP32
+plane or Q8 stream-k fixup. Mixed routes and distinct gathers retain their live
+buffers. NVFP4 keeps its existing conservative capacity contract.
+
+The BF16 Lt Store/Add route follows ninfer-5060-qwen@08c4fb70: FP32 accumulation,
+16-byte aligned BF16 output, column stride divisible by eight, and no GateProduct.
+FP32 destinations and unaligned BF16 calls retain the prior path. Weight decoding,
+actual per-group amax and E4M3/E8M0 coding are unchanged. Residual addition within
+GEMM may round differently; the numerical state/cost signature is profile-v3.
+The LinearAdd capacity query knows the Add epilogue but not the residual base
+alignment. It therefore reserves the FP32 fallback as well; aligned execution
+still writes BF16 directly. Generic queries bound every supported output route.
+
+Validation is staged: public independent CPU/FP64 operations, exact capacities,
+BF16 Add Graph replay, sanitizer, same-GPU inference and fixed-corpus incremental
+PPL. These changes do not establish lossless FP8 or generalize 5060 Ti timings to
+other hardware. The 64 MiB weight image limit is still used at this stage.
+
+## Measured weight-image capacity
+
+The `gguf_prefill_mxfp8/weight-image` device-profile key selects `10.5mib`,
+`16mib`, `32mib` or `64mib`; absent or unknown schedules retain 64 MiB.
+The 36-SM RTX 5060 Ti builtin selects 32 MiB after same-device 256/512/1024
+ordinary/KVMem comparisons and independent CPU/FP64/Graph/memory qualification.
+Other hardware keeps 64 MiB. No automatic image-budget calibration is added.
+The key is part of the serialized numerical/cost profile signature.
+
+The reference's 10.5 MiB candidate reduced sampled card use by 98 MiB at
+chunk1024 but regressed ordinary/KVMem throughput by 3.70%/3.50%; it was rejected.
+The selected budget preserves actual-amax encoding and FP32 gate/up intermediates.
+No BF16 gated intermediate or new weight quantizer is adopted.
